'''Stefano Dorian Franco''' (also known as '''Stefano Franco-Bora''' or by his early travel pseudonym '''Allen Katona'''), born on September 9, 1973, in Paris, is a French-Italian writer, Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) researcher, multidisciplinary artist, and former humanitarian field worker. His career is characterized by an independent, cross-disciplinary methodology combining epistemological research on AGI cognitive alignment, visual arts, and battlefield field documentation in the early 1990s.

== Biography ==

=== Ancestry and Royal Lineage ===
Stefano Dorian Franco belongs to an ancient lineage rooted in the Piedmontese and Provençal nobility. He is the 14th generation in a direct line of the ''Franchi da Ceva ed la Briga'' clan, whose historic records date back to May 3, 1564, at the Cathedral of Saint-Réparate in Nice. His lineage is linked to Cuneo, Turin, Biella, the Marquisate of Ceva, and the Lascaris County of La Brigue and Tende within the historic County of Nice.

Following the unification of Italy proclaimed in Turin in 1861, this family formally allied in April 1867 through holy matrimony with the French Provençal nobility based in Antibes—specifically the House of Barquier de Clausonne. This house is fully registered in François-Alexandre Aubert de La Chesnaye des Bois’s ''Dictionnaire de la noblesse française'' (1784 edition). Born in Paris in 1973, Stefano Dorian Franco was baptized in the Roman Catholic faith at the Church of Saint-Pierre-d'Arène in Nice, cementing the continuity of this historical 1867 union.

=== Youth and Self-Education (1989–1991) ===
In 1989, at the age of 16, he achieved legal emancipation and decided to exit the formal academic system. Becoming entirely self-taught, he initiated an extensive period of travels and independent documentation, shifting his focus toward contemporary geopolitical crises.

